{"toolCallId":"call_2676e11a1b144b36b50132b78b69b622","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables shorten the commands below:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the parser and the `output_text()` emitter to confirm both insertion points (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text\\(\\)|--json\\|-j' $S` prints the function definition and the parser case.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the default output as the regression baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 > $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt && wc -l < $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt` prints `16`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the JSON output as the second regression baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json > $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt && wc -l < $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` prints `36`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false` in the globals block (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet)` case arm to the argument parser, matching the shape of the `--json|-j` arm (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^    --quiet\\)' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the conflict check between the parse loop and the numeric validation, rejecting `--quiet` with `--json` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T007 Dispatch the one-line emitter in the output block so `QUIET` prints `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` instead of calling `output_text()` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` prints `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T008 Document `--quiet` in `show_help()` with its one-line contract (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` in the header OPTIONS block beside `--json, -j` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^#   --quiet' $S` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Diff the default output against the captured baseline (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt <(bash $S --loc 50 --files 2)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T011 Diff the JSON output against the captured baseline (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt <(bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Run the phase-system suite that drives the script through `--json` (`runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js`). Verify: `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Run the phase-validation suite that drives the script through `--json` fixtures (`runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js`). Verify: `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` exits 0.\n- [ ] T014 Exercise the error and edge paths: no arguments, invalid `--loc`, repeated `--quiet`, and `--quiet` with `--no-recommend-phases` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet; echo $?` prints the missing-input error on stderr and `1`, and `bash $S --quiet --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T015 Run the strict validator on this packet (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt` and `$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` exist and both diffs print nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`; ADR-001 there fixes the output label and the `--json` conflict rule\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA P0 row is closed only by the command in its text. A P1 row may close on a recorded reason in this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Check: `rg -c '^\\| REQ-' spec.md` prints `10`.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Check: `rg -n '^### ADR-001' plan.md` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Check: `bash --version | head -1` prints a 3.2 or newer version.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The edited script parses. Check: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The edit adds no whitespace damage. Check: `git diff --check -- $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The contradictory invocation is handled, not ignored. Check: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2; echo $?` prints a conflict message on stderr and `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new case arm follows the existing parser pattern. Check: `rg -n -A2 '^    --quiet\\)' $S` shows `QUIET=true` followed by `shift`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Check: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The quiet path prints exactly one line. Check: `bash $S --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested. Check: the T014 matrix ran and its four invocations printed the expected status.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated. Check: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-024 [P0] The default output did not move. Check: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt <(bash $S --loc 50 --files 2)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-025 [P0] The JSON output did not move. Check: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt <(bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json)` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed. Check: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.sh'` prints the single emitter.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for the changed script. Check: `rg -l 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'` lists every caller named in `plan.md`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The parser change carries adversarial cases for flag order, repetition and conflict, not just the happy path. Check: the T014 matrix names all four cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed. Check: `plan.md` affected-surfaces names the three axes.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence is pinned to the diff that made the change, not a moving branch range. Check: the completion note cites the commit that touches `$S`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Check: `rg -n 'password|token|secret|api[_-]?key' $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation still rejects non-integers. Check: `bash $S --loc abc >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks name the same flag and the same output label. Check: `rg -c -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Both documentation blocks describe the flag. Check: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `1` and `rg -n '^#   --quiet' $S` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baselines and any temporary output live under `scratch/` only. Check: `ls $P/scratch` lists `baseline-default.txt` and `baseline-json.txt` and nothing outside the packet changed.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` is cleaned before completion. Check: `ls $P/scratch` holds only `.gitkeep` and the two baselines the plan names.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 14 | [ ]/14 |\n| P1 Items | 10 | [ ]/10 |\n| P2 Items | 0 | [ ]/0 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verif