cratch/baseline-default.txt <(bash $S --loc 50 --files 2)` prints nothing and exits 0 | Unmet | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given `--quiet` and `--json` in either order, When the script runs, Then stderr names the conflict, stdout is empty, and the status is 1 | `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 >/tmp/q.out 2>/tmp/q.err; echo $?` prints `1`, `wc -c </tmp/q.out` prints `0`, and `/tmp/q.err` is non-empty | Unmet | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given a successful quiet run and an invalid quiet run, When each finishes, Then the status is 0 and 1 respectively | `bash $S --quiet --loc 50 --files 2; echo $?` prints `0`; `bash $S --quiet --loc abc; echo $?` prints `1` | Unmet | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-006 | Given the help text, When `--help` runs, Then it lists `--quiet` and states that only the recommended-level line prints | `bash $S --help \\| rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `1` and the surrounding lines name the one-line behavior | Unmet | - |\n| AC-007 | REQ-007 | Given the script header, When its OPTIONS block is read, Then `--quiet` sits beside the other flags | `rg -n '^#   --quiet' $S` prints one line | Unmet | - |\n| AC-008 | REQ-008 | Given `--quiet` with `--no-recommend-phases` or with `--phase-threshold 10`, When the script runs, Then the output is still exactly one line | `bash $S --quiet --no-recommend-phases --loc 1000 --files 20 --architectural --api --db \\| wc -l` prints `1` | Unmet | - |\n| AC-009 | REQ-009 | Given the same input, When it runs with and without `--quiet`, Then the level number and name agree | `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural \\| rg 'Recommended Level'` and `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` print the same `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)` | Unmet | - |\n| AC-010 | REQ-010 | Given an invalid input under `--quiet`, When the script fails, Then the existing stderr diagnostic still prints | `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null \\| rg -c 'ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer'` prints `1` | Unmet | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\nWrite `-` when the row is `Met` or `Unmet`. Write `ADR-NNN` when the row is\n`Waived` or `Superseded`, naming a decision record that exists in\n`decision-record.md`. A waiver naming an ADR that is not there fails validation:\nthe point of a waiver is that someone recorded the reasoning, so an unbacked\nwaiver is treated as an unmet criterion rather than as a pass.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:closure -->\n## 3. CLOSURE STATEMENT\n\n**Closeable:** No\n\nTen criteria are open and none is waived: the packet plans the change, so every row waits on the implementation and its command evidence. AC-003, AC-004 and AC-010 carry the risk — they are the three rows that would catch a quiet flag which broke the default report, silently outranked `--json`, or swallowed an input error.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:closure -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":2,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
