{"toolCallId":"call_da0a79bb63144d67a52879a7d2553d1d","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete the rows that do not apply. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables shorten the commands below:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the parser and the `output_text()` emitter to confirm both insertion points (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text\\(\\)|--json\\|-j' $S` prints the function definition and the parser case.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the default output as the regression baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 50 --files 2 > $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt && wc -l < $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt` prints `16`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the JSON output as the second regression baseline (`$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json > $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt && wc -l < $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` prints `36`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `QUIET=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT=false` in the globals block (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^QUIET=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T005 Add the `--quiet)` case arm to the argument parser, matching the shape of the `--json|-j` arm (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^    --quiet\\)' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T006 Add the conflict check between the parse loop and the numeric validation, rejecting `--quiet` with `--json` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T007 Dispatch the one-line emitter in the output block so `QUIET` prints `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` instead of calling `output_text()` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural` prints `Recommended Level: 3 (Full)`.\n- [ ] T008 Document `--quiet` in `show_help()` with its one-line contract (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` in the header OPTIONS block beside `--json, -j` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^#   --quiet' $S` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Diff the default output against the captured baseline (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt <(bash $S --loc 50 --files 2)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T011 Diff the JSON output against the captured baseline (`$S`). Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt <(bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json)` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Run the phase-system suite that drives the script through `--json` (`runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js`). Verify: `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-system.js` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Run the phase-validation suite that drives the script through `--json` fixtures (`runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js`). Verify: `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js` exits 0.\n- [ ] T014 Exercise the error and edge paths: no arguments, invalid `--loc`, repeated `--quiet`, and `--quiet` with `--no-recommend-phases` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet; echo $?` prints the missing-input error on stderr and `1`, and `bash $S --quiet --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T015 Run the strict validator on this packet (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt` and `$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt` exist and both diffs print nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`; ADR-001 there fixes the output label and the `--json` conflict rule\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA P0 row is closed only by the command in its text. A P1 row may close on a recorded reason in this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c '^\\| REQ-' spec.md` prints `10`.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n '^### ADR-001' plan.md` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version | head -1` prints a 3.2 or newer version.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The edited script parses. Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] The edit adds no whitespace damage. Verify: `git diff --check -- $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The contradictory invocation is handled, not ignored. Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2; echo $?` prints a conflict message on stderr and `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The new case arm follows the existing parser pattern. Verify: `rg -n -A2 '^    --quiet\\)' $S` shows `QUIET=true` followed by `shift`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The quiet path prints exactly one line. Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested. Verify: the T014 matrix ran and its four invocations printed the expected status.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated. Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] CHK-024 [P0] The default output did not move. Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-default.txt <(bash $S --loc 50 --files 2)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-025 [P0] The JSON output did not move. Verify: `diff $P/scratch/baseline-json.txt <(bash $S --loc 100 --files 3 --json)` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.sh'` prints the single emitter.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for the changed script. Verify: `rg -l 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled --glob '*.js' --glob '*.md'` lists every caller named in `plan.md`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The parser change carries adversarial cases for flag order, repetition and conflict, not just the happy path. Verify: the T014 matrix names all four cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed. Verify: `plan.md` affected-surfaces names the three axes.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Evidence is pinned to the diff that made the change, not a moving branch range. Verify: the completion note cites the commit that touches `$S`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'password|token|secret|api[_-]?key' $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation still rejects non-integers. Verify: `bash $S --loc abc >/dev/null 2>&1; echo $?` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks name the same flag and the same output label. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Both documentation blocks describe the flag. Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints `1` and `rg -n '^#   --quiet' $S` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baselines and any temporary output live under `scratch/` only. Verify: `ls $P/scratch` lists `baseline-default.txt` and `baseline-json.txt` and nothing outside the packet changed.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` is cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls $P/scratch` holds only `.gitkeep` and the two baselines the plan names.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 14 | [ ]/14 |\n| P1 Items | 10 | [ ]/10 |\n| P2 Items | 0 | [ ]/0 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] The architecture decision is recorded. Verify: `rg -n '^### ADR-001' plan.md` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] The ADR carries a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Proposed' plan.md` prints one line.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives are documented with a rejection reason. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Alternatives Rejected\\*\\*' plan.md` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] The quiet path adds no measurable cost (NFR-P01). Verify: a quiet run completes within the same second as the default run on the same input.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] The help text and the header block agree on the flag's contract. Verify: both name \"only the recommended-level line\" as the behavior.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":59,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":107}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/223-deepseek-final/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
